# Compiled-in exception list for the Morphy lemmatizer.
#
# Same format as the WNdb `{noun,verb,adj,adv}.exc` files — `surface lemma
# [lemma…]`, whitespace separated — so one parser serves both sources. Lines
# starting with `#` are a local extension; no real exception file has them.
#
# This table is the fallback used when `wordnet_dir` is unset or its exception
# files are unreadable. When WNdb is available its entries supersede these key
# by key (see `morphy::ExceptionTable::layered`).
#
# Two kinds of entry:
#
#   * inflection → base, for forms the detachment rules cannot reach
#     ("was be", "children child");
#   * self-mapping, which morphy reads as "this surface is already a lemma,
#     stop here" ("number number"). Those protect high-frequency words that a
#     detachment rule would otherwise mangle into a different real word —
#     `number` → `numb`, `her` → `he`, `bed` → `be`. The cost of a wrong
#     protection is one honest OOV entry; the cost of a wrong detachment is a
#     false dependency edge, so the trade is not symmetric.

